 # ASCII Art Skill
 
 Multiple tools for different ASCII art needs. All tools are local CLI programs or free REST APIs — no API keys required.
 
+## When to Use
+
+Load this skill when the user asks to:
+- Convert text to large ASCII banners or logos
+- Wrap messages in fun character art (cowsay, boxes)
+- Convert images (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WEBP) to ASCII art
+- Add decorative ASCII borders or frames around text
+- Generate QR codes as ASCII art
+- Create weather or moon phase ASCII graphics
+- Search for pre-made ASCII art of common subjects
+- Add terminal eye candy (rainbow text, metallic effects)
+
+## Not For
+
+- Creating actual images (PNG/JPG) → use `image_gen` or `stable-diffusion`
+- Drawing diagrams, architecture, or flowcharts → use `excalidraw` or `architecture-diagram`
+- Creating pixel art or sprites → use `pixel-art`
+- Formatting code or data tables → use markdown tables or code blocks
+- Animated graphics → ASCII art is static; for animation use `ascii-video`
+- High-fidelity image reproduction → ASCII is a low-resolution approximation
+
